{"units": [{"id": "amiantos-quote1", "translation": "And being carded by the dread salt sea, they are torn by the voiceless children of the undefiled one."}, {"id": "amiantos-word1", "translation": "being carded by the salt sea, dread things"}, {"id": "amiantos-word2", "translation": "of the undefiled one"}, {"id": "amiantos-word3", "translation": "of the salt sea"}, {"id": "amiantos-word4", "translation": "by the salt sea"}, {"id": "amida_see-orth1", "translation": "chamber pot"}, {"id": "amida_see-note1", "translation": "[erroneously for ἄμαλα [sheaves], which see]"}, {"id": "amida_see-word1", "translation": "sheaves"}, {"id": "amiktos-orth1", "translation": "unsociable, not joining in friendship"}, {"id": "amiktos-def1", "translation": "unsociable, not joining in friendship"}, {"id": "amiktos-quote1", "translation": "I think an unsociable cry is fitting in the city."}, {"id": "hamilla-orth1", "translation": "contest"}, {"id": "hamilla-def1", "translation": "contest"}, {"id": "hamilla-quote1", "translation": "with swift contests of wings"}, {"id": "amisthos-orth1", "translation": "unpaid, without reward"}, {"id": "amisthos-def1", "translation": "unpaid, without reward"}, {"id": "amisthos-quote1", "translation": "unbidden, unpaid song"}, {"id": "amisthos-quote2", "translation": "unpaid grief"}, {"id": "amistres-orth1", "translation": "Amistres (Persian proper name)"}, {"id": "amistres-def1", "translation": "Persian proper name"}, {"id": "amistres-note1", "translation": "But at Pers. 320 at the beginning of the trimeter it is Ἀμίστρις [Amistris], where Brunck has Ἀμηστρις [Amestris]."}, {"id": "amistres-quote1", "translation": "such as Amistres and Artaphrenes."}, {"id": "amistres-quote2", "translation": "Amistris,"}, {"id": "amistres-quote3", "translation": "Amestris"}, {"id": "ammignymi-orth1", "translation": "to mix in"}, {"id": "ammignymi-def1", "translation": "(for ἀναμίγνυμι [to mix in]) I mix in."}, {"id": "ammignymi-note1", "translation": "Thus I corrected what is in M: ἂν [if] (changed to αὖ [again]) μεμίζεται [will be mixed]."}, {"id": "ammignymi-note2", "translation": "] Λαν. ἄμμιγα ν [mixed] see under νὰ ἀναμίξ [to mix in]."}, {"id": "ammignymi-quote1", "translation": "and a black, groaning blow is mixed in."}, {"id": "ammignymi-word1", "translation": "to mix in"}, {"id": "ammignymi-word2", "translation": "if"}, {"id": "ammignymi-word3", "translation": "again"}, {"id": "ammignymi-word4", "translation": "will be mixed"}, {"id": "ammignymi-word5", "translation": "mixed"}, {"id": "ammignymi-word6", "translation": "to mix in"}, {"id": "amnemoneo-orth1", "translation": "to be unmindful"}, {"id": "amnemoneo-def1", "translation": "I am unmindful."}, {"id": "amnemoneo-quote1", "translation": "nor am I unmindful."}, {"id": "amnemon-orth1", "translation": "unmindful"}, {"id": "amnemon-def1", "translation": "unmindful"}, {"id": "amnemon-quote1", "translation": "to enemies and to those unmindful of the gods."}, {"id": "amoiros-orth1", "translation": "without a share"}, {"id": "amoiros-def1", "translation": "without a share"}, {"id": "amoiros-note1", "translation": "Thus I emended, as the meter demanded, for ἄμοιρος ἄκληρος ἐτύχθην [I was born without a share, without a lot], removing the gloss ἄκληρος [without a lot] and adding what the sense requires, μούνα [alone]."}, {"id": "amoiros-note2", "translation": "[At line 890 γ᾽ ἀμοίρου [at least without a share] is corrupt from γαμόρῳ [to the landowner], which see]"}, {"id": "amoiros-quote1", "translation": "without a share of the great plains."}, {"id": "amoiros-quote2", "translation": "but without a share of white-robed garments, I alone was born."}, {"id": "amoiros-word1", "translation": "I was born without a share, without a lot"}, {"id": "amoiros-word2", "translation": "without a lot"}, {"id": "amoiros-word3", "translation": "alone"}, {"id": "amoiros-word4", "translation": "at least without a share"}, {"id": "amoiros-word5", "translation": "to the landowner"}, {"id": "amolgos-orth1", "translation": "darkness"}, {"id": "amolgos-def1", "translation": "darkness"}, {"id": "amolgos-quote1", "translation": "the darkness of the holy night."}, {"id": "amomphetond_see-orth1", "translation": "blameless"}, {"id": "amomphetond_see-note1", "translation": "[erroneously for ἀμεμφή τόνδ' [this blameless one]. See ἀμεμφής [blameless].]"}, {"id": "amomphetond_see-word1", "translation": "this blameless one"}, {"id": "amomphetond_see-word2", "translation": "blameless"}, {"id": "amomphos-orth1", "translation": "blameless"}, {"id": "amomphos-def1", "translation": "blameless"}, {"id": "amomphos-def2", "translation": "who has nothing to be blamed for"}, {"id": "amomphos-note1", "translation": "Thus Robortellus for ἄμορφον [shapeless]."}, {"id": "amomphos-quote1", "translation": "Nevertheless, though you are blameless, I choose you for the city."}, {"id": "amomphos-quote2", "translation": "How am I to be considered blameless by you?"}, {"id": "amomphos-quote3", "translation": "to speak ill of one's neighbors, though blameless, beyond what is just."}, {"id": "amomphos-word1", "translation": "shapeless"}, {"id": "amos-orth1", "translation": "my"}, {"id": "amos-def1", "translation": "my"}, {"id": "amos-note1", "translation": "The tragedians used it for ἐμός [my] when the first syllable needed to be long, on which see what I said in the Lexicon Sophocleum p. 26."}, {"id": "amos-note2", "translation": "It was wrongly inserted in M at Eum. 440: ἑστίας ἁμῆς πέλας [near my hearth], as if the fifth foot of the trimeter needed a spondee. Correctly ἐμῆς [my] in the copies. But correctly at line 311, where in M ἐπινωμᾷ στάσις ἅμα [the faction distributes together] is read, it has been restored to ἀμά [our], unless one prefers ἁμά [our], which is said for ἡμετέρα [our], with Canter: in which sense it is very uncertain that the tragedians used ἁμός [our], as I showed in the Lexicon Sophocleum. ἁμός [our] everywhere in M."}, {"id": "amos-quote1", "translation": "May the gods grant that my adversary now prosper."}, {"id": "amos-quote2", "translation": "O my much-wept race of Oedipus."}, {"id": "amos-quote3", "translation": "my head, beaten and all-wretched."}, {"id": "amos-quote4", "translation": "by the will of our hands."}, {"id": "amos-quote5", "translation": "because of my marriage."}, {"id": "amos-quote6", "translation": "my ancient race."}, {"id": "amos-quote7", "translation": "near my hearth,"}, {"id": "amos-quote8", "translation": "the faction distributes together"}, {"id": "amos-word1", "translation": "my"}, {"id": "amos-word2", "translation": "my"}, {"id": "amos-word3", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "amos-word4", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "amos-word5", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "amos-word6", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "amos-word7", "translation": "our"}, {"id": "amochthi-orth1", "translation": "without toil"}, {"id": "amochthi-def1", "translation": "without toil"}, {"id": "amochthi-quote1", "translation": "They thought they would rule without toil and by force."}, {"id": "ampelos-orth1", "translation": "vine"}, {"id": "ampelos-def1", "translation": "vine"}, {"id": "ampelos-note1", "translation": "See μάχλος [luxuriant]."}, {"id": "ampelos-quote1", "translation": "this delight of the ancient vine."}, {"id": "ampelos-quote2", "translation": "luxuriant vine."}, {"id": "ampelos-word1", "translation": "luxuriant"}, {"id": "ampempo_see-orth1", "translation": "to send up"}, {"id": "ampempo_see-word1", "translation": "to send up"}, {"id": "ampecho-orth1", "translation": "to surround"}, {"id": "ampecho-def1", "translation": "I surround"}, {"id": "ampecho-quote1", "translation": "hearing of the dishonor of my child, about her body, of the garments that clothe her."}, {"id": "ampipto-orth1", "translation": "to fall upon"}, {"id": "ampipto-def1", "translation": "I fall upon"}, {"id": "ampipto-note1", "translation": "Thus Canter for ἂν πίπτει [would fall]."}, {"id": "ampipto-quote1", "translation": "and it falls upon me from the slaughter."}, {"id": "ampipto-word1", "translation": "would fall"}, {"id": "amplakein-orth1", "translation": "to err"}, {"id": "amplakein-def1", "translation": "to err"}, {"id": "amplakein-quote1", "translation": "how I erred in these things."}, {"id": "amplakein-quote2", "translation": "But what if I have erred in these things without justice?"}, {"id": "amplakema-orth1", "translation": "error"}, {"id": "amplakema-def1", "translation": "error"}]}